\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl408\slmult1\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf4 H1.1. (Populism + Polarization) When exposed to the same FIMI campaign, States with a polarized environment and increased levels of populism and distrust in traditional media under common measurements are more vulnerable.\
H1.2. (Social Media Usage + Polarization) When exposed to the same FIMI campaign, States with a polarized environment and high levels of social media usage under common measurements are more vulnerable.\
H1.3. (Aging societies + Polarization) When exposed to the same FIMI campaign, States with a polarized environment and aging demographics are more vulnerable.\
\cf0 \
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf4  Polarization = (GINI * 0.3) + ((WVSQ57(i) * 0.5 + WVSQ61(i) * 0.5 ) * 0.3) +  (WVSQ117(i) * 0.4)\
\
WVSQ57 = Less Trust = Higher number\
WVSQ61= Less Trust = Higher number\
WVSQ117 = Less Trust = Higher number\
GINI = Higher inequality = Higher number\
\
Therefore = The higher the number, the lower the trust and more polarization. \
\
Exported as: H1_POL\
\
No correlation was found between levels of democracy and this model of polarization, meaning you can have a highly polarized country that is both democratic or authoritarian. \
\
