\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
H2.1. (High Trust in Media  + Low Media Literacy) When exposed to the same FIMI campaign, states with a population with reduced digital media literacy and high trust on traditional media are more vulnerable. \
\
H2.2. (Low Trust in Media  + Low Media Literacy) When exposed to the same FIMI campaign, states with a population with reduced digital media literacy and low trust on traditional media are more vulnerable.\
\
H2.3. (High use of Social Media  + Low Media Literacy) When exposed to the same FIMI campaign, states with a population with reduced digital media literacy and high use of social media are more vulnerable.\
\
I present an adapted Media Literacy Index \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl408\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4 v-MLI(i)= (Education(i)*0.40) + \
(E-Participation(i) * 0.10) + (MediaAccess(i)*0.40) + (IT(i)*0.10)\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
Education is composed of reading comprehension and tertiary education levels.\
\
For Media Access, we adapt the following:\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi720\sl408\slmult1\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf4  Media Access (i) = (Internet (i) * 0.3) + ((100-(\uc0\u916  Internet(i) / max\u916  Internet(i)))* 0.2) + (Internet_Freedom(i)*0.2) + (Mobile_Access (i) * 0.3) )\
\pard\tx566\tx1133\tx1700\tx2267\tx2834\tx3401\tx3968\tx4535\tx5102\tx5669\tx6236\tx6803\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
Internet = Higher number means higher population use.\
Internet Difference = Higher number means more abrupt growth, which would mean more vulnerability, therefore we use 100 - to invert. \
Internet freedom = Higher number means more freedom.\
Mobile Access = Higher number means more access.\
\
This CSV File is provided independently.\
\
Then we calculate the index, we keep a proportional number for those issues which data is missing. \
\
The results show that there is correlation between Media literacy and democracy levels because of the strong relevancy of press freedom, but this is not fixed, since you have authoritarian countries \
\
